    "title": "Preguntas con to be + números",
    "rule": "Para preguntar con 'to be', pon el verbo al inicio: Are you...? / Is he...? / Where are you from? La edad se dice con 'be', no con 'have': I am 25 years old. El número de teléfono y la dirección usan 'My... is'.",
    "examples": [
      "How old are you? — I am 25 years old.",
      "Where are you from? — I am from Colombia.",
      "Where do you live? — I live in Bogotá.",
      "My phone number is 555-1234."
    ],
    "commonMistakes": [
      "I have 25 years → I am 25 years old",
      "How old do you have? → How old are you?"
    ]
  },
  "pronunciationTip": "No confundas -teen con -ty: thirteen (13) /θɜːrˈtiːn/ suena con el acento al final, thirty (30) /ˈθɜːrti/ con el acento al inicio.",
